 and *n.q.* (not quantified), left out\nof the plots and statistics, and their number is given under the title. Use the **Linear / Log**\nbuttons for the scale.\n\n**How to read it**\n\n- **Differences between the study groups** are what you are after; the QCs should be tight.\n- **Many replaced values** in a group mean the compound is mostly below the LLOQ there; its\n  average is then driven by the replacement values, so look at the measured values only (the\n  exported statistics and report 4.6.1 use measured values only).\n\n## 4.7 QC samples in acquisition order\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<div id=\"htmlwidget-3138257321a2b0ba7796\" style=\"width:100%;height:425px;\" class=\"plotly html-widget\"></div>\n<script type=\"application/json\" data-for=\"htmlwidget-3138257321a2b0ba7796\">{\"x\":{\"visdat\":{\"786477ec6028\":[\"function () \",\"plotlyVisDat\"]},\"cur_data\":\"786477ec6028\",\"attrs\":{\"786477ec6028\":{\"alpha_stroke\":1,\"sizes\":[10,100],\"spans\":[1,20],\"type\":\"scatter\",\"mode\":\"lines+markers\",\"x\":[28,40,121,178,216,240],\"y\":[0.01,0.01,0.01,0.01,0.10000000000000001,0.10000000000000001],\"name\":\"QC1\",\"text\":[\"<b>QC1_QC_B1_28<\\/b><br>QC1 · batch 1 · inj. 28<br>conc. 0.01 (Detected: LLOQ/2)\",\"<b>QC1_QC_B1_40<\\/b><br>QC1 · batch 1 · inj. 40<br>conc. 0.01 (Detected: LLOQ/2)\",\"<b>QC1_QC_B2_121<\\/b><br>QC1 · batch 2 · inj. 121<br>conc. 0.01 (Detected: LLOQ/2)\",\"<b>QC1_QC_B2_178<\\/b><br>QC1 · batch 2 · inj. 178<br>conc. 0.01 (Detected: LLOQ/2)\",\"<b>QC1_QC_B3_216<\\/b><br>QC1 · batch 3 · inj. 216<br>conc. 0.1 (Detected: LLOQ/2)\",\"<b>QC1_QC_B3_240<\\/b><br>QC1 · batch 3 · inj. 240<br>conc. 0.1 (Detected: LLOQ/2)\"],\"hoverinfo\":\"text\",\"line\":{\"color\":\"#0072B2\",\"width\":1},\"marker\":{\"color\":[\"white\",\"white\",\"white\",\"white\",\"white\",\"white\"],\"size\":8,\"line\":{\"color\":\"#0072B2\",\"width\":1.5}},\"inherit\":true},\"786477ec6028.1\":{\"alpha_stroke\":1,\"sizes\":[10,100],